- op: discuss  # ccf2
  at: '2026-06-11T15:57:08Z'  # ccf2
  by: agent  # ccf2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ccf2
  clock: 3  # ccf2
  nonce: ccf2  # ccf2
  message: "Fixed in PR #4185 (merged to dev as 3218484b76). resolve_workdir in BOTH scripts/bakeoff-broad and scripts/bakeoff-deep now prefix-isolates its session auto-discovery: each delegates to the already-correct _find_latest_session(prefix=<own-mode>) instead of scanning broad-/deep- together and trusting a full-string lexicographic sort (which let a stale deep-* out-sort a fresh broad-* since 'd'>'b', and let bakeoff-deep adopt a foreign broad-*). The duplicated scan loop and the false 'lexicographic sort works' comment are gone. POSITIVE EVIDENCE the invariant holds: tests/test_bakeoff_resolve_workdir_prefix.py asserts resolve_workdir never returns a foreign-mode session — broad ignores a newer deep-*, deep ignores a newer broad-*, each falls through to base when only the foreign prefix is present, and the latest own-prefix session wins (5 cases green; 347 bakeoff tests pass, no regression). This is the strategy's Wave-0 gate 'workdir-resolution unit test (broad/deep prefix filtering)'."  # ccf2
